# Indexing Inventory

_No `DayData` type exists in the current code. Its role is implemented by the
column table in `AllSeries`._

## 1-indexed storage

| Structure | Valid indexes | Index 0 |
|---|---:|---|
| `PopData` per-person vectors: `status`, `agegrp`, `cond`, `duration`, `variant`, all history/day fields, `ring`, `sdcase`, `quar`, `vaxstatus`, and `vax` | `1..popn` | Reserved and never a person, even where its initialized value looks meaningful (for example `UNEXPOSED`). `popz == popn + 1`. |
| `PopData::all_idx` values | Values are `1..popn` | The vector itself is ordinarily zero-indexed; it stores 1-based person IDs. |
| `Variant::names`, `ModelParams::variant_names` | real variants: `1..N` | `"none"` sentinel; `Variant{1}` must be `"base"`. |
| `ModelParams::infectparams` | real variants: `1..N` | Dummy `InfectParams`; direct lookup uses the raw `Variant` ID. |
| `ProgressionSet::progression` | real variants: `1..N` | Dummy `Progression`; progression never uses variant zero. |
| `InfectParams::recovery_immunity` | variant IDs: `1..N` | Allocated as zero/default immunity for variant `"none"`; it is directly indexed by raw `Variant` IDs. |
| `Vax::names`, `VaxSet::names`, `VaxSet::params` | real vaccines: `1..N` | `"none"` plus a dummy `Vaxparam`; `VaxSet::at()` rejects zero. |
| `Ring::names`, `RingTraits::ring_names`, `RingTraits::pct_of_population` | real rings: `1..N` | Empty-string/zero-value sentinel. |
| `RingTraits::out_ring_prob[ring][agegrp]` | both dimensions: `1..N` / `1..5` | Outer ring zero and inner age-group zero are unused. |
| `Model::ring_members`, `Model::ring_lengths` outer dimension | real rings: `1..N` | Reserved. Inner `ring_members[ring]` vectors are ordinary zero-indexed lists containing 1-based person IDs. |

`AgentView` enforces this rule: it rejects person IDs below 1 or above `popn`. See [population.h](/Users/lewislevin/code/epi_sim/src/population.h:36) and [ring_traits.h](/Users/lewislevin/code/epi_sim/src/ring_traits.h:12).

## Series: mixed indexing

`AllSeries` owns a private outer vector of columns. Six `SeriesBlock` values
identify contiguous ranges for `now_status`, `new_status`, `now_vax`,
`new_vax`, `now_variant`, and `new_variant`. Each range has a descriptor with
its base column and strides.

```text
cols[column_index(block, subject_id, age_bucket, ring_id)][simulation_day]

column_index = block_base
             + subject_id * (ring_count * bucket_count)
             + ring_id * bucket_count
             + age_bucket
```

| Dimension | Indexing |
|---|---|
| `block` | Zero-based `SeriesBlock` identifier. Block order is status now/new, vaccine now/new, then variant now/new. |
| `subject_id` | Raw `Status`, `Vax`, or `Variant` ID. Slot 0 exists as the respective `"none"` sentinel and is normally not reported. Real values begin at 1. |
| `ring_id` | `0` is valid: `RING_ALL`, the all-rings aggregate. Real rings are `1..N`. |
| `age_bucket` | Fully zero-based. `0` is valid and means `total`; `1..5` are the concrete age buckets. |
| `simulation_day` | 1-based. Every leaf vector has `day_cnt + 1` elements; day 0 is unused. |

The physical order is `block -> subject -> ring -> age bucket`, with age
bucket fastest. The public printing and CSV-writing paths iterate days
`1..day_cnt`. The vaccinated-total materializer retains the unused day-zero
slot when it sums non-sentinel vaccine-brand columns. See
[series.h](/Users/lewislevin/code/epi_sim/src/series.h) and
[series.cpp](/Users/lewislevin/code/epi_sim/src/series.cpp).

## Zero-based or compact parameter storage

| Structure | Indexing and mapping |
|---|---|
| `Config::age_dist` / `Model::age_dist` | Ordinary 5-element, zero-based vector: positions map to the five concrete age groups in order. |
| `PopData::agegrp_parts` | Ordinary zero-based 5-element vector of apportioned counts. |
| `PopData` history arrays (`VariantHist`, `VaxHist`, `SickdayHist`, `RecovdayHist`, `TestdayHist`, `VaxdayHist`) | Ordinary zero-based fixed arrays. `count` is a length, not an index; the most recent non-full entry is at `count - 1`. |
| `InfectParams::sendrisk` | Zero-based by disease duration, including index 0. The simulation directly uses `sendrisk[duration]`. |
| `InfectParams::recvrisk` | Dense, zero-based 5-element age table: use `zidx(agegrp)` (`agegrp - 1`). |
| `ProgressionFactors::riskadjust` | Dense zero-based six-element table indexed by `Progressionmap`: recover, nil, mild, sick, severe, dead. |
| `ProgressionTree::entries` | Ordinary zero-based packed-entry vector. |
| Packed progression condition/outcome arrays | Conditions are projected with `zidx(condition)` (`nil..severe` → `0..3`); outcomes use zero-based `Progressionmap` directly (`0..5`). |
| `Vaxparam::infectfactor` | Compact zero-based vector. Position `variant_id - 1`; it intentionally omits `"none"`. |
| `Vaxparam::effectiveness` outer vector | Compact zero-based vector. Position `vaxstatus - 1`: first, full, booster. It omits `Vaxstatus::none`. |
| `Vaxparam::effectiveness` inner vector | Compact zero-based vector. Position `variant_id - 1`; it omits `"none"`. |
| `VaxSched::vaxesincluded`, `PerVaxSpec::alternate`, `filtervec`, `pattern` | Ordinary zero-based lists. Stored `Vax`/`Agegrp` values may themselves be 1-based IDs. |
| `VaxSchedSet::schedules` | Ordinary zero-based list. |
| `SocialParams::contactfactors` | Zero-based `4 × 5`: condition row `zidx(nil..severe)`, age column `zidx(agegrp)`. |
| `SocialParams::touchfactors` | Zero-based `6 × 5`: `touch_map()` produces rows 0–5; age column is `zidx(agegrp)`. |
| `SocialDistancing::contact_delta`, `touch_delta`, `include_ages`, and `sd_cases` | Ordinary zero-based vectors. `SDCase` IDs are assigned as vector position + 1, so runtime access uses `sd_cases[zidx(sdcase)]`. |
| `GeoData` columns | Ordinary zero-based, row-aligned vectors; this is CSV input rather than JSON. |
| `Model::caldays`, `Model::indoor_seq` | Ordinary zero-based vectors. Simulation day `d` uses `zidx(d)`. |

`ProgressionTree::entry_index` is the main mixed table: `[zidx(agegrp)][duration]`. Its age dimension is zero-based, but duration/day 0 is deliberately unused; valid progression days are `1..DURATIONLIM`. See [parameters.h](/Users/lewislevin/code/epi_sim/src/parameters.h:132) and [parameters.cpp](/Users/lewislevin/code/epi_sim/src/parameters.cpp:215).

## Identifier-zero semantics

| Identifier | Value 0 |
|---|---|
| `Agegrp` | `"unknown"` sentinel; not a real age-table index. |
| `Status` | `"none"` sentinel; real statuses begin at 1. |
| `Condition` | `"uninfected"` is a valid state, but parameter tables exclude it and use `zidx(nil..severe)`. |
| `Variant` | `"none"` sentinel; generally invalid during simulation. |
| `Vax` | `"none"` sentinel. |
| `Ring` | Unassigned/empty sentinel. |
| `SDCase` | `"none"` sentinel. |
| `Vaxstatus` | Valid `"none"` state, but vaccine-effectiveness tables omit it. |
| `Progressionmap` | Valid zero-based index; no sentinel. |

`idx(x)` preserves an ID, while `zidx(x)` converts a real one-based ID to its compact zero-based table position. See [helpers.h](/Users/lewislevin/code/epi_sim/src/helpers.h:43).

The JSON loaders establish the sentinel-aligned variant, vaccine, and ring tables; the runtime paths verify the compact vaccine-factor mapping and use direct numeric lookups. See [parameters.cpp](/Users/lewislevin/code/epi_sim/src/parameters.cpp:84), [parameters.cpp](/Users/lewislevin/code/epi_sim/src/parameters.cpp:375), and [parameters.cpp](/Users/lewislevin/code/epi_sim/src/parameters.cpp:571).
